        <DataSetName>PurchaseOrder</DataSetName>
        <Top>1.54458in</Top>
        <Left>0.40467in</Left>
        <Height>4.54305in</Height>
        <Width>7.65537in</Width>
        <ZIndex>2</ZIndex>
        <Style>
          <Border>
            <Style>None</Style>
          </Border>
        </Style>
      </Tablix>
      <Textbox Name="Textbox2">
        <CanGrow>true</CanGrow>
        <KeepTogether>true</KeepTogether>
        <Paragraphs>
          <Paragraph>
            <TextRuns>
              <TextRun>
                <Value xml:space="preserve">                                                                                                    </Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                  <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>Special Terms and Conditions</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>11pt</FontSize>
                  <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
            </TextRuns>
            <Style>
              <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
            </Style>
          </Paragraph>
          <Paragraph>
            <TextRuns>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>
1.	</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>All Prices are on DDP basis</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                  <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>, i.e. Prices are inclusive of all taxes and duties, regulatory charges, sea-freight, inland freight, sales tax, etc. The goods will be delivered at the buyer’s premises with no extra charge

2.	</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>Sales tax invoice will be provided by the supplier for the entire applicable amount where applicable. Sales tax is included in the price of this contract

3.	Income tax will be deducted as per the prevailing law, unless the supplier provides supporting evidence not to withhold income tax.

4.	Goods declaration and certificate of origin will be provided for all imported items. It must be ensured that the Goods declaration is in the name of the supplier and not any other party.

5.	Prior approval from buyer for the delivery of the items.</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                  <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>

6.	All items delivered will have at the minimum 12 months left for expiry. In case any item has a shorter expiry, the purchaser reserves the right to reject that delivery and return the items to the supplier.

7.	The supplier commits to lift back any items that for which the purchaser sends a written request. 

8.	In case any item delivered by the supplier and stocked by the purchaser nears its expiry date, the purchaser will return this item to the supplier or have it replaced with a longer expiry item. In case of returns, the purchaser will ensure that items are returned at least 75 days prior to expiry.

9.	All items delivered will undergo inspection and acceptance of any delivery will be given after inspection is approved. In case of rejection, the items will be lifted back by the supplier.

10.	No price escalation will be permitted.
11.	No extra charges will be paid for customs clearance, freight, installation, or any other charge.

12.	The supplier will be responsible to inform us of any global alert, recall, support discontinuation from the manufacturer as well as timely execute any action required, in both the pre and post warranty period.</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
            </TextRuns>
            <Style>
              <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
            </Style>
          </Paragraph>
          <Paragraph>
            <TextRuns>
              <TextRun>
                <Value />
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
            </TextRuns>
            <Style>
              <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
            </Style>
          </Paragraph>
          <Paragraph>
            <TextRuns>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>13.	The supplier indemnifies Gate Healthcare, Evercare Hospitals and EHF, its directors, employees and management against any claim of any nature that may arise due to malfunction of equipment.

14.	The supplier will provide requisite training to nurses, technicians, doctors, biomedical staff, and all other relevant staff. 

15.	The supplier warrants that all laws and regulations pertaining to environment, labour, licenses, taxes, etc will be followed and complied with. 

16.	The supplier commits that they do not employ any child labour and adhere to the local labour laws. In addition, the supplier accepts the terms of our Code of Conduct

17.	According to sub section 5 of section 153 read with clause 47A to the part IV of Second Schedule to the Income Tax Ordinance, 2001, the implications of Income Tax withholding shall not apply to Commercial Importer wherein the goods are sold in the same condition as they were when imported. Based on this clause, Party - 2 will provide import documents, including the GD issued in the name of Party - 2 (being importer itself) to certify that the import was made by supplier itself and sold without any alteration. In addition, Party - 2 will provide an undertaking to the client who states that the import was made by supplier itself and sold without any alteration.

18.	In addition to above, the supplier will provide an undertaking to the client stating that no sales tax should be deducted in accordance to Section 5 ‘Exclusions’ Special Procedure Withholding Rules, 2007, which states that the implication of Sales Tax Withholding shall not apply to Commercial Importers.


19.	Payment will be made through cross cheque in favor of “</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>=First(Fields!Party_Name.Value, "PurchaseOrder")</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                  <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
              <TextRun>
                <Value>”. Payment terms will be as follows:
i.	After 30 days of Submitting Invoicewith Delivery Challan comments : 30 days to be linked with PO dash board

</Value>
                <Style>
                  <FontFamily>times New Roman</FontFamily>
                  <FontSize>9pt</FontSize>
                </Style>
              </TextRun>
            </TextRuns>
            <Style>
              <TextAlign>Left</TextAlign>
            </Style>
          </Paragraph>
        </Paragraphs>
        <rd:DefaultName>Textbox2</rd:DefaultName>
